Her book is an amusing and readable romp through the school year at a state primary school in a well-to-do village.
It follows the friendships and feuds among the mothers as they foist themselves upon (or are reluctantly inveigled into) the life and fundraising escapades of the school, while poor relationships, health issues and jobs all weave unexpected twists into the plot. As the characters jostle for position, allegiances change and hierarchies shift.
